From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:18:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/28] fix(midea): map J15 dock error codes from firmware
 table

Station error 100 is CollectDust, a dock activity rather than a fault.
Don't switch the robot to ERROR for it; the dock status still shows
EMPTYING via status byte 36.

103 (dirty water tank full) and 104 (dirty water tank missing) now feed
the dirty water tank dock component like 152 does, and have their own
messages. 111 is the wash tray being full, 112 the robot's tank being
full and 148 a duct switch error, replacing the previous texts.

Also map the remaining named station codes that showed up as unknown:
102, 108, 110, 113, 115, 116, 118, 119, 120, 130, 132, 133, 138, 144,
145 and 153. The dustbag codes 11/12/13 stay; they are unreachable on
this firmware but harmless.

Based on static analysis of the StationErrors table; untested on the
robot. Wording of the less obvious codes is derived from the internal
names only.

